[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Select Mozc as your input method in the uim preferences.

For an X11 session, set the following environment variables before
starting applications:

export GTK_IM_MODULE=uim
export QT_IM_MODULE=uim
export XMODIFIERS=@im=uim

For example, place these settings in ~/.xinitrc before the command
that starts your desktop or window manager.

Install the uim input module matching your applications:
  GTK3: textproc/uim-gtk3
  GTK4: textproc/uim-gtk4
  Qt5:  textproc/uim-qt5
  Qt6:  textproc/uim-qt6

For XIM applications, start uim-xim if your session does not
already start it:

%%LOCALBASE%%/bin/uim-xim &

uim-xim requires uim built with X11 support.
For Wayland sessions, use the setup appropriate to your compositor.

The Mozc server starts automatically when needed.
EOM
}
]
